    "user_request_original": "Optimize a 36-layer alternating Ta2O5/SiO2 dielectric filter on fused silica substrate at 0 degree incidence with unpolarized light. Layer sequence: Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2, Ta2O5, SiO2 (18 Ta2O5 layers, 18 SiO2 layers). All layer thicknesses bounded between 15 nm and 355 nm. Initialize optimization population with bimodal distribution: 50% of layers sampled from 20-60 nm range, 50% from 150-300 nm range. Optimize to maximize average transmittance in 420-700 nm passband while minimizing average transmittance in 355-365 nm stopband, 1030-1080 nm stopband, and at 355 nm single wavelength. Use gradient-based thickness optimizer with step-size constraints. Report best target score, valid candidate count, tightest margin, and thickness arrays for all candidates. Canonical user controls: incidence angles 0 degrees. polarization unpolarized. wavelength intervals 355-355 nm, 355-365 nm, 420-700 nm, 1030-1080 nm. soft objectives: high average transmittance in 420-700 nm; low average transmittance at 355 nm; low average transmittance in 355-365 nm; low average transmittance in 1030-1080 nm. behaviors to suppress or avoid: high transmittance at 355 nm; high transmittance in 355-365 nm; high transmittance in 1030-1080 nm; high loss in 420-700 nm. manufacturing constraints: maximum 36 layers; layer thickness range 20-350 nm.",
